criteria:
Inclusion Criteria:

* Diagnosis of a congenital or acquired neuromotor disorder;
* Age between 4 and 8 years at the time of enrollment;
* Modified Ashworth Scale (MAS) score ≤2;
* Manual Ability Classification System (MACS) level I-IV;
* Sufficient ability to understand the proposed activities;
* Signed informed consent for participation in the study;
* Compliance with all study procedures and the overall study duration.

Exclusion Criteria:

* Severe sensory deficits;
* Severe comorbidities and/or behavioral or cognitive disorders that prevent adequate compliance with the treatment;
* Functional orthopedic surgery and/or botulinum toxin injection in the upper limbs within the 6 months preceding the study;
* Susceptibility to epileptic episodes.
